            <div xml:id="d925">

                <pb facs="0861" n="853" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg853"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-24T13:00:00+03:00">May 24, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received May 24—11:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>168. In view of the frequent complaints of the local press previously reported
                    (although not shared in informed official circles) as to our alleged slowness in
                    furnishing aid to Turkey and other small countries and of my lack of any
                    definite information on the subject, I should appreciate being informed more
                    specifically as to the nature and extent of the aid mentioned in your telegram
                    No. 72, May 17, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="55" xml:id="d925-f1"/> as having been already
                    extended to Turkey under the Lease-Lend Act and as to any arrangements for such
                    aid in future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
